,59,90,28],[33375,12.6,1952,55,94,28],[33668,43.6,2015,64,92,24],[33669,36.4,1973,58,92,22],[33670,18.8,1973,50,86,28],[33671,13.6,1973,46,83,27],[33672,12.6,1973,47,87,26],[33673,12.2,1973,50,90,26]],"links":[["Teton County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/montana/teton-county"],["ARC or PLC in Teton County","/arc-plc/montana/teton-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the Teton County record runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 20 grids. November to December came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years, the most of any pair. In 2025, May to June ran 50% of normal on the middle of the grids, while January to February ran 153%. Grid 33071 had its driest year in 1973 at 51%.</p>"}
